    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209998": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in the Clinical Science Program in the Department of Psychology",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Assistant Professor in the Clinical Science Program in the Department of Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor in the Clinical Science Program in the Department of Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Proposed Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Department 00143 - Psychology Department City Salt Lake City, UT Track Tenure Track New Position to Begin 07/01/2027 Details CLINICAL SCIENTIST SPECIALIZING IN DISSEMINATION & IMPLEMENTATION SCIENCE . The Department of Psychology at the University of Utah invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor faculty position in our Clinical Science program. We are seeking applicants with research and teaching interests in Dissemination and Implementation (D&I) Science. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in implementation science approaches that seek to improve access to evidence-based behavioral health interventions, reduce health disparities, and strengthen healthcare systems. Examples of research emphases that would fit the position include the development, dissemination, implementation, adaptation, scaling-up, or sustainment of evidence-based psychological and behavioral interventions across clinical, healthcare, educational, community, and/or public health settings. We particularly welcome candidates whose work also focuses on rural, frontier, youth, and/or underserved communities. Applicants with a strong research record, high-quality clinical training from a clinical science perspective, and a commitment to community-engaged translational research are especially encouraged to apply. License eligibility, skills in quantitative methods, and experience securing or demonstrated potential for external funding are highly valued. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an active research program, contribute to graduate and undergraduate teaching, and help develop curriculum, training opportunities, and community partnerships that support community-engaged research. Applications from individuals whose research complements existing departmental strengths in psychotherapy processes, prevention and early intervention, health behavior interventions, social determinants of health, health disparities, developmental and systems-level science, and community-engaged translational research are particularly encouraged. This new faculty position reflects the Department’s strategic investment in Dissemination & Implementation Science and aligns with the University of Utah’s Impact 2030 initiative, which emphasizes improving health, strengthening communities, and translating research discoveries into measurable societal benefit. The Department of Psychology provides an exceptionally collaborative environment for interdisciplinary research. The Clinical Science Program is a long-standing member of the Academy of Psychological Clinical Science and has been continuously accredited by the APA since 1954. The program has a history of generative collaborations among faculty specializing in clinical neuropsychology, clinical child and family psychology, clinical health psychology, and adult psychopathology. Faculty also collaborate extensively with colleagues in the department’s Cognition and Neural Sciences, Developmental, Social, and Quantitative Psychology programs. Beyond the department, faculty benefit from extraordinary opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across one of the nation’s fastest-growing academic medical centers. Potential collaborators span the Spencer Fox Eccles School of Medicine, Huntsman Mental Health Institute, College of Nursing, College of Social Work, College of Health, Department of Population Health Sciences, School of Medicine, Veterans Affairs Salt Lake City Health Care System, Primary Children’s Hospital, Center for Safe and Healthy Families, the Behavioral Health Innovation and Dissemination Center ( BHIDC ), the Huntsman Cancer Institute, and numerous federally funded centers and institutes. The University of Utah has made substantial institutional investments in team science, implementation research, community-engaged scholarship, biomedical informatics, learning health systems, and health equity, creating exceptional opportunities for investigators pursuing innovative translational research. The University of Utah is located in Salt Lake City nestled in the foothills of the Wasatch Mountains. With an enrollment of 38,000 students (and growing), it is the flagship university for the state of Utah and a member of the Association of American Universities ( AAU ). The university administration provides strong support for faculty research and teaching in the Psychology Department. Please submit statements of research and teaching interests, a curriculum vitae, three representative reprints or preprints of publications, and contact information for three individuals who will provide letters of recommendation. Questions about the position should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Anu Asnaani, at anu.asnaani@psych.utah.edu. Review of applications will begin October 5, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Open Date 08/04/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN01552CF Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Example of Research 1 Example of Research 2 Example of Research 3 List of References Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only Cover Letter University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209991": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer) - Lecturer Track - DOQ",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer) - Lecturer Track - DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer) - Lecturer Track - DOQ Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer) - Lecturer Track - DOQ Department 00196 - Health & Kinesiology City Salt Lake City, UT Track Non Tenure Track New Position to Begin July 1, 2027 Details University of Utah, College of Health Department of Health & Kinesiology Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer), Lecturer Track – DOQ The Department of Health & Kinesiology in the University of Utah’s College of Health invites applications for two Career-Line teaching faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor (Lecturer) or Associate Professor (Lecturer), commensurate with qualifications and experience. Successful candidates will contribute to the department’s undergraduate teaching mission through excellence in instruction, student mentorship, curriculum development, and university and professional service. Candidates should have the ability to teach and contribute to curriculum development in at least two of the following courses, or similar courses within their area of expertise: · Exercise Physiology ( KINES 3091) · Exercise Physiology Laboratory ( KINES 4301) · Physical Activity Epidemiology ( KINES 3670) · Community-Based Capstone Experience ( KINES 4900) · Foundations in Kinesiology ( KINES 2500) · Applied Functional Anatomy ( KINES 3092) · Biomechanics ( KINES 3093) · Motor Control, Motor Learning, and Development ( KINES 3550) · Sport Sociology ( KINES 2600) · Exercise/Health Psychology ( KINES 3350) · Applied Behavior Change ( HEDU 4250 and HEDU 6260) · Exercise Programming ( KINES 4465) · Applied Exercise Programming ( KINES 4466) · Training and Planning ( KINES 4690) · Exercise in Special Populations , including cancer and diabetes ( KINES 4680) Position Responsibilities The primary responsibility of this position is teaching undergraduate courses in both in-person and online formats within the Department of Health & Kinesiology. The department prepares future leaders, practitioners, and scholars and serves approximately 1,700 students across its bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. Undergraduate class sizes typically range from 25 to 75 students. The standard teaching load is four courses in the fall semester and four courses in the spring semester, with opportunities for summer teaching potentially available. In addition to teaching, faculty members are expected to: · Develop and maintain high-quality undergraduate courses and curricula. · Mentor and support students in their academic and professional development. · Participate in curriculum and program development. · Contribute to university, department, and professional service, including faculty governance. · Engage in activities that support the mission and strategic priorities of the Department of Health & Kinesiology and the College of Health. The University of Utah’s College of Health is leading the transformation in health care—from primarily caring for people when they are sick to empowering them to be healthy, active, and resilient through proactive, preventive, and rehabilitative care. Through innovative research and by preparing the next generation of practitioners, the college is on a mission to add more years to our lives and MORE LIFE to those years. This position will contribute directly to that mission through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and service. The University of Utah’s Career-Line faculty structure provides opportunities for renewable contracts and multi-year appointments. Minimum and Preferred Qualifications Minimum Qualifications · Master’s degree in kinesiology or related discipline. · Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching. · Ability to effectively teach and mentor undergraduate students. Preferred Qualifications · Doctoral degree in kinesiology or a related discipline. · Experience teaching courses in one or more of the subject areas identified above. · Experience with curriculum development and/or course design. · Experience teaching in both in-person and online environments. We encourage applications from individuals who are enthusiastic about teaching and mentoring the next generation of leaders in health and kinesiology. The College of Health and the Department of Health & Kinesiology are committed to fostering a work environment in which people feel safe, valued, welcomed, and respected. About the University of Utah and Department of Health & Kinesiology The University of Utah is a Carnegie Research I institution located in Salt Lake City, in the foothills of the majestic Wasatch Range of the Rocky Mountains. The University of Utah academic and health sciences campuses are adjacently located, facilitating seamless trans- and interdisciplinary research collaborations. The Department of Health and Kinesiology is part of the College of Health and University of Utah Health Sciences. The Department of Health & Kinesiology’s undergraduate and graduate program is on the leading edge of training future scholars, health professionals and leaders in health sciences, with approximately 1,700 students registered in bachelors, masters and PhD degree programs. These programs are accredited by the National Academy of Kinesiology and Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs, with the graduate program consistently ranking as one of the top programs in the country. Faculty in the Department of Health and Kinesiology have access to the College of Health’s state-of-the-science research facility, a resource-rich environment managed by a full-time lab manager and containing seven research laboratories: · Exercise Intervention Laboratory · Exercise Testing Laboratory · Wet Laboratory · Sleep, Circadian Physiology and Cognition Suite · Metabolic Kitchen; Mobility and Stability Laboratory · Musculoskeletal Biomechanics Laboratory Faculty also have access to 24 core research facilities available at the University ( cores.utah.edu ) and the opportunities to collaborate with other entities across the academic and health sciences campuses including the Clinical and Translational Sciences Institute, Center on Aging, Huntsman Mental Health Institute, Huntsman Cancer Institute, the Responsible Artificial Intelligence Initiative, Digital Health Initiative, College of Health Community Outreach and Engagement, among others. Faculty in the Department of Health and Kinesiology have afforded success in obtaining extramural funding such as support from NIH , CDC , DOD and NSF . University of Utah and Community The University of Utah’s distinguished partnership with the International Olympic Committee ( IOC )—one of only eleven such partnerships worldwide—underscores its international leadership in applied health research, human performance, and athlete health and well-being. With the 2034 Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games returning to Salt Lake City, the Health & Kinesiology Program is uniquely positioned to advance and showcase innovative research, education, human performance, and community health and wellness initiatives associated with the Games. This environment provides exceptional opportunities for faculty to develop interdisciplinary collaborations and contribute to research and programs with local, national, and global impact. Life in Salt Lake City, Utah and the surrounding area is exceptional. With easy access to eight world-class ski resorts, as well as hiking, biking, camping, backpacking, fishing, and exploring in nearby canyons and in the spectacular red-rock country of southern Utah. Ten National Parks are within a day driving distance of the University. Salt Lake City also offers professional symphony, ballet, modern dance, opera and theater performances, art galleries, world-class restaurants, and professional sports. Application Instructions Applicants must apply online at: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209659 Applicants should submit the following materials: 1. Cover letter (maximum one page) 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Most recent teaching evaluations , if available 4. Teaching statement (maximum two pages) addressing: · Teaching philosophy · Qualifications to teach at least two of the courses listed above · Long-term vision for the position 5. List of three professional references , including names and contact information Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled . On-campus interviews are expected to take place early in the spring semester. Anticipated start date: July 1, 2026 Inquires Inquires may be sent to: Dr. Tim Brusseau Professor and Chair Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health Tel: 801.587.7900 tim.brusseau@utah.edu OR Dr. Traci Thompson Associate Professor (Clinical) Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health Traci.Thompson@utah.edu University of Utah Health University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Application Instructions Applicants must apply online at: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209659 Applicants should submit the following materials: 1. Cover letter (maximum one page) 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Most recent teaching evaluations , if available 4. Teaching statement (maximum two pages) addressing: · Teaching philosophy · Qualifications to teach at least two of the courses listed above · Long-term vision for the position 5. List of three professional references , including names and contact information Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled . On-campus interviews are expected to take place early in the spring semester. Anticipated start date: July 1, 2027 Inquires Inquires may be sent to: Dr. Tim Brusseau Professor and Chair Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health Tel: 801.587.7900 tim.brusseau@utah.edu OR Dr. Traci Thompson Associate Professor (Clinical) Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health Traci.Thompson@utah.edu Open Date 09/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04137F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Teaching Evaluations List of References Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209989": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Assistant Professor Department 00196 - Health & Kinesiology City Salt Lake City, UT Track Tenure Track New Position to Begin July 1, 2027 Details University of Utah, College of Health Department of Health & Kinesiology Assistant Professor – Behavioral Science & Community Health Tenure-Line Faculty Position The Department of Health & Kinesiology in the College of Health at the University of Utah invites applications for a Tenure Track Assistant Professor whose research aligns with the Department’s Behavioral Science & Community Health Research Theme. We seek an innovative and collaborative scholar with a strong or emerging program of research focused on understanding and improving health and health behaviors across individuals, populations, communities, organizations, and/or health systems. The Behavioral Science & Community Health Research Theme advances understanding of the multilevel factors that influence health and health behaviors and develops, evaluates, disseminates, implements, and sustains approaches to improve health across diverse populations and settings. Areas of Research Interest Areas of research interest may include, but are not limited to: · Designing and testing health promotion, disease prevention, and chronic disease self-management across the lifespan; · Understanding health behavior (e.g., physical activity, nutrition, weight management, sleep) change and the behavioral, social and structural, or environmental determinants of health; · Dissemination and implementation of science focused on community and clinical strategies to improve the reach, accessibility, adoption, implementation and sustainability of evidence-based interventions; · Digital, mobile, LLM -based, AI-enabled, adaptive, or other innovative approaches to health behavior change; · Community-engaged and community-based participatory research; · Supporting priority population strategies to improve health outcomes among populations experiencing disproportionate disease burden or barriers to health-promoting resources; and · Multilevel interventions spanning individuals, families, organizations, communities, health care systems, or policy environments. Candidates whose scholarship bridges behavioral science and other areas of departmental or University strength are particularly encouraged to apply. We welcome a range of methodological approaches and do not expect candidates to work across all areas listed above. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: · Establish and maintain an innovative, collaborative, and externally funded program of research; · Disseminate research findings through high-quality peer-reviewed publications and presentations at national and international scientific meetings; · Contribute to collaborative and interdisciplinary research within the Department, College of Health, University of Utah Health, and broader University community; · Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses consistent with departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise; · Mentor undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students and contribute to the Department’s research-intensive MS and PhD programs; and applied MS program; · Contribute to the intellectual and scholarly activities of the Behavioral Science & Community Health Research Theme; and · Participate in appropriate service to the Department, College, University, profession, and/or community. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have: · Earned doctorate (PhD, DrPH, ScD, or equivalent) in kinesiology, health promotion, behavioral science, public health, psychology, nutrition, implementation science, or another discipline relevant to behavioral science and community health by the start date; · Evidence of the potential to develop an independent and impactful program of research; · A record of peer-reviewed scholarship appropriate to career stage; · Evidence of, or strong potential for, obtaining competitive extramural research funding; · Evidence of, or potential for, excellence in teaching and mentoring students; and · Strong potential to contribute to collaborative and interdisciplinary research. Preferred Qualifications · Postdoctoral research experience About the University of Utah and Department of Health & Kinesiology The University of Utah is a Carnegie Research I institution located in Salt Lake City, in the foothills of the majestic Wasatch Range of the Rocky Mountains. The University of Utah academic and health sciences campuses are adjacently located, facilitating seamless trans- and interdisciplinary research collaborations. The Department of Health and Kinesiology is part of the College of Health and University of Utah Health Sciences. The Department of Health & Kinesiology’s undergraduate and graduate program is on the leading edge of training future scholars, health professionals and leaders in health sciences, with approximately 1,700 students registered in bachelors, masters and PhD degree programs. These programs are accredited by the National Academy of Kinesiology and Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs, with the graduate program consistently ranking as one of the top programs in the country. Faculty in the Department of Health and Kinesiology have access to the College of Health’s state-of-the-science research facility, a resource-rich environment managed by a full-time lab manager and containing seven research laboratories: · Exercise Intervention Laboratory · Exercise Testing Laboratory · Wet Laboratory · Sleep, Circadian Physiology and Cognition Suite · Metabolic Kitchen · Mobility and Stability Laboratory · Musculoskeletal Biomechanics Laboratory Additionally, faculty have access to 24 core research facilities available at the University (cores.utah.edu) and the opportunity to collaborate with other entities across the academic and health sciences campuses including the Clinical and Translational Sciences Institute, Center for Metabolic Health, Center on Aging, Huntsman Mental Health Institute, Huntsman Cancer Institute, the Responsible Artificial Intelligence Initiative, Digital Health Initiative, College of Health Community Outreach and Engagement, among others. Faculty in the Department of Health and Kinesiology have afforded success in obtaining extramural funding such as support from NIH , CDC , DOD and NSF . University of Utah and Community The University of Utah’s distinguished partnership with the International Olympic Committee ( IOC )—one of only eleven such partnerships worldwide—underscores its international leadership in applied health research, human performance, and athlete health and well-being. With the 2034 Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games returning to Salt Lake City, the Health & Kinesiology Program is uniquely positioned to advance and showcase innovative research, education, human performance, and community health and wellness initiatives associated with the Games. This environment provides exceptional opportunities for faculty to develop interdisciplinary collaborations and contribute to research and programs with local, national, and global impact. Life in Salt Lake City, Utah and the surrounding area is exceptional. With easy access to eight world-class ski resorts, as well as hiking, biking, camping, backpacking, fishing, and exploring in nearby canyons and in the spectacular red-rock country of southern Utah. Ten National Parks are within a day driving distance of the University. Salt Lake City also offers professional symphony, ballet, modern dance, opera and theater performances, art galleries, world-class restaurants, and professional sports. Application Instructions Applicants must apply online at: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209645 Applicants should submit the following materials: 1. Cover letter (maximum one page) describing the applicant’s interest in the position and alignment with the Department of Health & Kinesiology and Behavioral Science & Community Health Research Theme; 2. Curriculum vitae; 3. Research statement (maximum three pages) describing the applicant’s prior scholarship, current research program, and plans for developing an independent and externally funded program of research; 4. Teaching and mentoring statement (maximum two pages) describing the applicant’s teaching philosophy, relevant experience, and approach to mentoring undergraduate and graduate students; and 5. List of three professional references , including names and contact information. Letters of recommendation may be requested at a later stage of the search. Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start date: July 1, 2027 Inquires Inquires may be sent to: Dr. Tim Brusseau Professor and Chair Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health Tel: 801.587.7900 tim.brusseau@utah.edu OR Dr. Tanya Halliday Associate Professor Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health tanya.halliday@utah.edu University of Utah Health University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Application Instructions Applicants must apply online at: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209645 Applicants should submit the following materials: 1. Cover letter (maximum one page) describing the applicant’s interest in the position and alignment with the Department of Health & Kinesiology and Behavioral Science & Community Health Research Theme; 2. Curriculum vitae; 3. Research statement (maximum three pages) describing the applicant’s prior scholarship, current research program, and plans for developing an independent and externally funded program of research; 4. Teaching and mentoring statement (maximum two pages) describing the applicant’s teaching philosophy, relevant experience, and approach to mentoring undergraduate and graduate students; and 5. List of three professional references , including names and contact information. Letters of recommendation may be requested at a later stage of the search. Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start date: July 1, 2027 Inquires Inquires may be sent to: Dr. Tim Brusseau Professor and Chair Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health Tel: 801.587.7900 tim.brusseau@utah.edu OR Dr. Tanya Halliday Associate Professor Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health tanya.halliday@utah.edu Open Date 09/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04136F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement List of References Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209988": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer) - Lecturer Track - DOQ",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer) - Lecturer Track - DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer) - Lecturer Track - DOQ Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer) - Lecturer Track - DOQ Department 00196 - Health & Kinesiology City Salt Lake City, UT Track Non Tenure Track New Position to Begin July 1, 2027 Details University of Utah, College of Health Department of Health & Kinesiology Assistant/Associate Professor (Lecturer), (Lecturer) Track, Career-Line Position The Department of Health & Kinesiology at the University of Utah is seeking to hire a 0.75 FTE , Career-Line (non-tenure) faculty member with expertise in Emergency Medical Services ( EMS ). This full-time appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor (Lecturer) or Associate Professor (Lecturer) , depending on qualifications and experience. This is a long-term, renewable position within the University’s Career-Line faculty structure, with the potential for multi-year contracts. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching, program development, and community engagement in a dynamic and growing academic environment. Position Responsibilities The primary responsibility of this position is teaching undergraduate courses in both in-person and online formats within the Department of Health & Kinesiology. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to teach and contribute to curriculum development in areas including: Emergency Medical Services Core Courses o Pathophysiology for EMS – HEDU 4450 o AEMT – HEDU 5970 o EMS Ethics Div & Law – HEDU 4400 o EMS Planning and Eval – HEDU 4950 · EMS Pharmacology ( HEDU 3033) · Medical Terminology ( HEDU 3030) · Anatomy and Physiology ( HEDU 4660) · Other EMS -related and/or Paramedic coursework as appropriate In addition to teaching, the successful candidate will: · Contribute to curriculum and program development within Emergency Medical Services. · Oversee and support experiential learning opportunities. · Develop and maintain relationships with community and industry partners. · Participate in university, department, college, and professional service, including faculty governance. · Contribute to the ongoing growth and development of the EMS program. The standard teaching load is four courses in the fall semester and four courses in the spring semester. Opportunities for summer teaching may also be available. In addition to teaching, all faculty members are expected to participate in university and professional service, including faculty governance. The Department of Health & Kinesiology prepares future leaders, practitioners, and scholars and serves approximately 1,700 students across its bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. Undergraduate class sizes typically range from 25 to 75 students. Emergency Medical Services Program Emergency Programs, housed within the Department of Health & Kinesiology, oversees curriculum and instruction for the Bachelor of Science in Emergency Medical Services ( EMS ) degree. The program currently has approximately 260 declared majors and serves approximately 500 non-major students annually through emergency programs academic courses. The successful candidate will join a growing program and contribute to the education and preparation of the next generation of EMS professionals and leaders. Minimum Qualifications: · Master’s Degree or Higher Required · EMS Certification Preferred · Demonstrated Potential for Excellence in Teaching · Evidence of Ability to Contribute to Program Development · Experience or Demonstrated Ability to Engage with Community Partners We encourage applications from individuals who are enthusiastic about teaching and mentoring the next generation of leaders in health and kinesiology. The College of Health and the Department of Health & Kinesiology are committed to fostering a work environment in which people feel safe, valued, welcomed, and respected. About the College of Health The University of Utah’s College of Health is leading the transformation in health care—from primarily caring for people when they are sick to empowering them to be healthy, active, and resilient through proactive, preventive, and rehabilitative care. Through innovative research and by preparing the next generation of practitioners, the college is on a mission to add more years to our lives and MORE LIFE to those years. This position will contribute directly to that mission through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and service. The University of Utah’s Career-Line faculty structure provides opportunities for renewable contracts and multi-year appointments. About the Department of Health & Kinesiology The Department of Health and Kinesiology is part of the College of Health and University of Utah Health Sciences. The Department of Health & Kinesiology’s undergraduate and graduate program is on the leading edge of training future scholars, health professionals and leaders in health sciences, with approximately 1,700 students registered in bachelors, masters and PhD degree programs. These programs are accredited by the National Academy of Kinesiology and Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs, with the graduate program consistently ranking as one of the top programs in the country. The University of Utah is a Carnegie Research I institution located in Salt Lake City, in the foothills of the majestic Wasatch Range of the Rocky Mountains. The University of Utah academic and health sciences campuses are adjacently located, facilitating seamless trans- and interdisciplinary research collaborations. Faculty in the Department of Health and Kinesiology have access to the College of Health’s state-of-the-science research facility, a resource-rich environment managed by a full-time lab manager and containing seven research laboratories: · Exercise Intervention Laboratory · Exercise Testing Laboratory · Wet Laboratory · Sleep, Circadian Physiology and Cognition Suite · Metabolic Kitchen · Mobility and Stability Laboratory · Musculoskeletal Biomechanics Laboratory Faculty also have access to 24 core research facilities available at the University ( cores.utah.edu ) and opportunities to collaborate with other entities across the academic and health sciences campuses including the Clinical and Translational Sciences Institute, Center on Aging, Huntsman Mental Health Institute, Huntsman Cancer Institute, the Responsible Artificial Intelligence Initiative, Digital Health Initiative, College of Health Community Outreach and Engagement, among others. Faculty in the Department of Health and Kinesiology have afforded success in obtaining extramural funding such as support from NIH , CDC , DOD and NSF . University of Utah and Community The University of Utah’s distinguished partnership with the International Olympic Committee ( IOC )—one of only eleven such partnerships worldwide—underscores its international leadership in applied health research, human performance, and athlete health and well-being. With the 2034 Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games returning to Salt Lake City, the Health & Kinesiology Program is uniquely positioned to advance and showcase innovative research, education, human performance, and community health and wellness initiatives associated with the Games. This environment provides exceptional opportunities for faculty to develop interdisciplinary collaborations and contribute to research and programs with local, national, and global impact. Life in Salt Lake City, Utah and the surrounding area is exceptional. With easy access to eight world-class ski resorts, as well as hiking, biking, camping, backpacking, fishing, and exploring in nearby canyons and in the spectacular red-rock country of southern Utah. Ten National Parks are within a day driving distance of the University. Salt Lake City also offers professional symphony, ballet, modern dance, opera and theater performances, art galleries, world-class restaurants, and professional sports. Application Instructions Applicants must apply online at: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209588 Applicants should submit the following materials: 1. Cover letter (maximum one page) 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Most recent teaching evaluations , if available 4. Teaching statement (maximum two pages) addressing: · Teaching philosophy · Qualifications to teach at least two of the courses listed above · Long-term vision for the position 5. List of three professional references , including names and contact information Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start date: July 1, 2027 Inquires Inquires may be sent to: Dr. Tim Brusseau Professor and Chair Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health Tel: 801.587.7900 tim.brusseau@utah.edu University of Utah Health University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Application Instructions Applicants must apply online at: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209588 Applicants should submit the following materials: 1. Cover letter (maximum one page) 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Most recent teaching evaluations , if available 4. Teaching statement (maximum two pages) addressing: · Teaching philosophy · Qualifications to teach at least two of the courses listed above · Long-term vision for the position 5. List of three professional references , including names and contact information Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start date: July 1, 2027 Inquires Inquires may be sent to: Dr. Tim Brusseau Professor and Chair Department of Health & Kinesiology College of Health Tel: 801.587.7900 tim.brusseau@utah.edu Open Date 09/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04135F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Teaching Evaluations List of References Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only Applicant Document - Other University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
