    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209972": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Clinical) Neuro-Ophthalmology",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Assistant Professor (Clinical) Neuro-Ophthalmology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor (Clinical) Neuro-Ophthalmology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Assistant Professor (Clinical) Neuro-Ophthalmology Department 00267 - Ophthalmology-Services City Salt Lake City, UT Track Non Tenure Track New Position to Begin 07/28/2026 Details NEURO - OPHTHALMOLOGIST The Departments of Ophthalmology and Visual Sciences and Neurology at the University of Utah, John A. Moran Eye Center are actively seeking a neuro-ophthalmologist. This position will be primarily in clinical care delivery. Responsibilities also include medical student, resident and fellow teaching in the clinic. Duties will include Neuro-Ophthalmology, with ophthalmology or neurology to be determined by applicant training and preference. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with experience. This is a full-time clinical faculty position in an academic setting. Candidates must have completed an accredited ophthalmology residency program and be Ophthalmology board certified or board eligible by the American Board of Ophthalmology or a Neurology residency program and be board certified or board eligible by the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology and have completed a fellowship in neuro-ophthalmology. Clinical experience in outpatient neurology or ophthalmology would be beneficial. Please visit the following quick link to apply for this position: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/206114 Inquiries may be sent to tiffany.hobbs@hsc.utah.edu The University of Utah is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer and does not discriminate based upon race, national origin, color, religion, sex, age, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, status as a person with a disability, genetic information, or Protected Veteran status. Individuals from historically underrepresented groups, such as minorities, women, qualified persons with disabilities and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. To inquire about the University’s nondiscrimination or affirmative action policies or to request disability accommodation, please contact: Director, Office of Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action, 201 S. Presidents Circle, Rm 135, (801) 581-8365. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students from diverse backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education for historically underrepresented students. Statement of Values: The University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. The U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Special Instructions box: Three letters of recommendation are required. Please solicit three letters of recommendation on your behalf and have these letters emailed to Tiffany.Hobbs@hsc.utah.edu and addressed to: Jeff Pettey, M.D., M.B.A. Chair, Department of Ophthalmology 65 Mario Capecchi Drive Salt Lake City, UT 84132 Open Date 07/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04093F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * One measure of faculty diversity at the School of Medicine is the proportion of faculty members who come from a rural background. Did you graduate high school from a town with less than 10,000 persons? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209934": {
      "title": "Pediatric Endocrinologist, Las Vegas, NV/ Rank Dependent on Qualifications",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Pediatric Endocrinologist, Las Vegas, NV/ Rank Dependent on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Pediatric Endocrinologist, Las Vegas, NV/ Rank Dependent on Qualifications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Pediatric Endocrinologist, Las Vegas, NV/ Rank Dependent on Qualifications Department 00853 - Pediatric Endocrinology City Las Vegas, NV Track Track Dependent on Qualifications New Position to Begin Details The Division of Pediatric Endocrinology & Diabetes in the Department of Pediatrics, University of Utah School of Medicine is seeking board eligible/board certified pediatric endocrinologists to join and help grow pediatric endocrinology and diabetes services at Intermountain Nevada Children’s Hospital in Las Vegas, Nevada. The pediatric endocrinologists will work as part of a collaborative multidisciplinary team that includes advanced practice providers, certified diabetes care and education specialists, dietitians, nurses, and other clinical support staff. This position provides comprehensive medical management to children and adolescents with diabetes and other endocrine-related diagnoses in both outpatient and inpatient settings. This is primarily a clinical position with opportunities for teaching, quality improvement, program development, and research or other scholarly activities based on the candidate’s interests. The physicians will collaborate closely with pediatric primary care physicians, hospitalists, intensivists, and other pediatric medical and surgical subspecialists. New fellows as well as experienced pediatric endocrinologists are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities include providing evidence-based, patient- and family-centered pediatric endocrinology and diabetes care in outpatient and inpatient settings, and collaborating with the multidisciplinary team to improve access, clinical outcomes, safety, efficiency, and patient experience. The Las Vegas pediatric endocrinology team will also have opportunities to collaborate with the University of Utah Division of Pediatric Endocrinology & Diabetes, a large academic group that includes 14 pediatric endocrinologists, 4 advanced practice providers, and 4 pediatric endocrinology fellows. This collaboration provides opportunities for shared clinical expertise, education, quality improvement, scholarly activity, and program development. Intermountain Health is building a new children’s hospital in Las Vegas, with significant plans to develop and grow specialized pediatric care for the children in the region. Together with the Division of Pediatric Endocrinology and Diabetes, this is an opportunity to join and build transformative pediatric care regionally. Las Vegas is a dynamic and affordable community with easy access to year-round outdoor activities including climbing, road and mountain biking, hiking, professional sports, and world-class entertainment. The city’s economy is robust and expanding, and in addition to the famous social and cultural downtown, there are great communities ideal for families. Qualified candidates must be Board Eligible/Board Certified in Pediatrics and Pediatric Endocrinology. Medical licensure in the states of Utah and Nevada are required at the time of hire. The selected candidate will receive a faculty appointment in the Department of Pediatrics on the Adjunct, Clinical, or Tenure Track at the academic level commensurate with experience and qualifications. The University of Utah/Department of Pediatrics offers a generous benefits package including a variety of medical and dental plans from which to choose (with in-network coverage throughout the Las Vegas region), exceptional retirement plans, and paid time off. A complete list of benefits can be viewed at https://www.benefits.utah.edu . Interested individuals can apply for the position at https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/209813 . Cover letter and curriculum vitae are required. For additional information about the position, please contact Vana Raman, Division Chief, Pediatric Endocrinology and Diabetes, at vana.raman@hsc.utah.edu . The University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. The U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Open Date 09/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04140F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you Board Eligible or Board Certified in Pediatrics? yes no * Are you board eligible or board certified in Pediatric Endocrinology? Yes No * Are you legally authorized to work in the United States? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B status)? Yes No * One measure of faculty diversity at the School of Medicine is the proportion of faculty members who come from a rural background. Did you graduate high school from a town with less than 10,000 persons? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
