    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/208713": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean of Global and Urban Underserved Medical Education",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Assistant Dean of Global and Urban Underserved Medical Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Dean of Global and Urban Underserved Medical Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter and List of References when submitting your application. Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Track and Rank dependent upon qualifications. Department 00203 - School of Medicine-Dean City Salt Lake City, UT Track Track Dependent on Qualifications New Position to Begin Once Filled. Details Global medical education exchanges at the Spencer Fox Eccles School of Medicine at the University of Utah ( SFESOM ) are currently established at multiple sites with five memos of understanding in place at medical schools in Ghana, Rwanda, Peru, Colombia, and South Korea. Urban underserved clinical rotations at the SFESOM are currently established within a network of student-led clinics (SLCs) and longitudinal integrated clerkship ( LIC ) sites. These clinical experiences are anchored by robust graduate certificate programs, creating a longitudinal thread of didactics and applied learning through scholarly research and community engagement experiences throughout the mission-driven MD program. Further development in thematically aligned medical education programs that reflect the SFESOM’s mission is anticipated, particularly with the anticipated opening of University of Utah Health’s West Valley Hospital. Job Summary The SFESOM seeks a physician for the position of Assistant Dean of Global and Urban Underserved Medical Education ( ADGUME ). In partnership with the Senior Associate Dean of Rural, Underserved, and Regional Medical Education and the Assistant Dean of Rural Medical Education and Pathways Innovation, the ADGUME collaborates with faculty and staff to design and implement innovative strategies for global and urban underserved medical education, including integration within the broader context of faculty-led educational programs targeting medically underserved populations at the SFESOM and the broader University of Utah community. The ADGUME supports the University of Utah’s goals and mission and acts as a catalyst between departments, faculty, staff, students, and external entities. The ADGUME will report directly to the Senior Associate Dean of Rural, Underserved, and Regional Medical Education. This newly created position holds salary support of 0.5 FTE . Roles & Responsibilities ● Develops and implements a vision for global and urban underserved medical education programs in partnership with local, regional, and global medical education leaders, ensuring alignment with the SFESOM mission and educational goals. ● Oversees all aspects of the global and urban underserved medical education program, including ensuring full compliance with internal policies and accreditation-related, regulatory, and legal standards. ● Represents the SFESOM global and urban underserved medical education programs to internal and external parties, including University offices, local/regional/international partners, national medical education consortia, and accrediting bodies. ● Serves as a spokesperson for the SFESOM global and urban underserved medical education programs to premedical advisors, educational institutions, legislative and regional governing bodies, donors, and the broader academic community, strengthening relationships that support program development and sustainability. ● Works together with the broader University of Utah community, including the Health Sciences colleges, the School of Dentistry, and other programs in the SFESOM to coordinate global and urban underserved medical education programs, including opportunities for interprofessional education. ● Provides leadership and mentorship to faculty and staff engaged in global and urban underserved medical education teaching threads in the curriculum, including supporting faculty director(s) and staff engaged in the graduate certificate programs in Global and Tribal, Rural, and Urban Underserved ( TRU ) Medicine and lecturing as a guest instructor in these and other programs. ● Provides leadership and mentorship to faculty and staff engaged in the selection, onboarding, engagement, education, and assessment of students involved in global and urban underserved medical education activities and career paths. ● Manages partnerships with international academic medical schools to facilitate medical student exchange and works closely with staff to manage all international electives for outgoing SFESOM medical students and all visiting international medical students, including all required credentialing and vetting for international visiting students. ● Works closely with staff to manage revenue-generating, fee-based credentialing and vetting services and functions for non-student international visitors (e.g., faculty, residents, researchers) participating in activities in UUH clinical environments (i.e., “Department-Sponsored International Visitors”) ● Leads and/or attends relevant operational, educational program, executive, interdisciplinary, and other relevant committee and council meetings ● Other duties as assigned Qualifications ● MD or DO degree from an accredited institution ● Completion of an ACGME -accredited residency ● Current board certification in a recognized medical specialty ● Eligibility for an unrestricted Utah physician and surgeon license (see DOPL requirements) ● Demonstrated leadership experience, with excellent interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work with various constituencies that will help further the global and urban underserved medical education programs at the SFESOM , including international partners ● Strong experience in medical education, including experience building an academic research program in global and/or underserved medical education ● Contemporary knowledge of the culture of academic medicine and understand the issues of wellness, diversity, academic performance that medical students face ● Previous experience in living and/or working in a global and/or urban underserved community is desirable How to Apply Interested candidates should submit an abbreviated curriculum vitae highlighting experience relevant to the position (3 pages or less), cover letter that includes a brief statement of qualifications, experience, interest, and intended approach in meeting the responsibilities of the position (2 pages or less), and names and contact information of three professional references. Internal candidates should also provide a letter of support from their academic department chair/division chief. Applications will be reviewed upon receipt. Please contact Michelle Hofmann for additional information or questions. All applications must be submitted online at: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/208404 Inquiries may be directed to: Michelle Hofmann, MD, MPH , MHCDS , Senior Associate Dean (Interim) Southern Utah Regional Medical Campus Spencer Fox Eccles School of Medicine at the University of Utah michelle.hofmann@hsc.utah.edu The University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. The U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Interested candidates should submit an abbreviated curriculum vitae highlighting experience relevant to the position (3 pages or less), cover letter that includes a brief statement of qualifications, experience, interest, and intended approach in meeting the responsibilities of the position (2 pages or less), and names and contact information of three professional references. Internal candidates should also provide a letter of support from their academic department chair/division chief. Applications will be reviewed upon receipt. Please contact Michelle Hofmann for additional information or questions. Open Date 09/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04109F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). One measure of faculty diversity at the School of Medicine is the proportion of faculty members who come from a rural background. Did you graduate high school from a town with less than 10,000 persons? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Applicant Document - Other University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
