    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/206116": {
      "title": "Department of Neurology, Division of Vascular Neurology seeking Neurocritical Care Specialist, Assistant Professor to Professor",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Department of Neurology, Division of Vascular Neurology seeking Neurocritical Care Specialist, Assistant Professor to Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Department of Neurology, Division of Vascular Neurology seeking Neurocritical Care Specialist, Assistant Professor to Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Department of Neurology, Division of Vascular Neurology seeking Neurocritical Care Specialist, Assistant Professor to Professor Department 01944 - Vascular City Salt Lake City, UT Track Track Dependent on Qualifications New Position to Begin Details Neurocritical Care Physician wanted to join the Department of Neurology at the University of Utah, Neurocritical Care Unit. The appointment may be at the assistant, associate, or professor rank in the career or tenure line program, depending upon qualifications. The Neurocritical Care Unit ( NCCU ) has 23 beds, portable Head CT scanning, invasive neuromonitoring, continuous EEG and state of the art technology (dedicated ultrasound and bronchoscopy equipment). The Unit has a total of 7 multi-disciplinary neurocritical care physicians. Staffing model will include dedicated NCCU in-house daytime and nighttime shifts as well as potential clinical responsibilities in telemedicine and emergency/acute care. The Unit has 9 Advanced Practice Clinicians (Nurse Practitioners and Physician Assistants) and an ACGME -accredited fellowship program. The unit is also staffed by neurology and neurosurgery residents, dedicated neurocritical nurses, nurse educators, respiratory therapists, dedicated pharmacists and patient-care technicians. There is a wide range of neurological and neurosurgical subspecialties together with advanced endovascular capabilities. Opportunities are available for clinical and/or basic research in the field. Applicants should be board certified or eligible for the neurocritical care boards. The University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. The U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. To apply, please submit your CV and cover letter to: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/203349 For questions, please contact Jae Hunt ( jae.hunt@hsc.utah.edu ). EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Requisition Number PRN04071F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B status)? Yes No Have you been trained in neurocritical care and critical care medicine in addition to residency training? (Open Ended Question) Are you fellowship trained AND Board Eligible/Board Certified in Critical Care? (Open Ended Question) Which critical care fellowship did you complete and which board are you eligible/certified in? UCNS / Neurocritical Care ACGME / Medical Critical Care ACGME / Surgical Critical Care ACGME / Anesthesia Critical Care Not fellowship trained in Critical Care / not board certified or eligible in Critical Care One measure of faculty diversity at the School of Medicine is the proportion of faculty members who come from a rural background. Did you graduate high school from a town with less than 10,000 persons? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/205429": {
      "title": "General OBGYN Division Director Rank/Title on Qualifications",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | General OBGYN Division Director Rank/Title on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help General OBGYN Division Director Rank/Title on Qualifications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank General OBGYN Division Director Rank/Title on Qualifications Department 00925 - General Obstetrics & Gyn Div City Salt Lake City, UT Track Track Dependent on Qualifications New Position to Begin 07/01/2027 Details The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Utah Health Sciences Center is seeking a board-certified Academic Specialist in Obstetrics and Gynecology to serve as Division Director. The ideal Division Director candidate will be an experienced, active clinician-scientist with strong leadership qualities, communication, and team-building skills. In this complex matrix model, the Division Director will have proven clinical skills, an outstanding teaching record, mentoring experience, and an established track record of NIH or other extramural research funding. The minimum academic rank required is Associate Professor. Documentation of effective leadership and communication skills from multiple sources will be expected in the application process. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Utah is an internationally recognized academic center in women’s health and child development. The Department is routinely ranked among the top 15 OB/ GYN departments for research in the US. The department currently holds 2 endowed chairs and is staffed by 48 clinicians/researchers, 55 midwives, nurse practitioners, and physician assistants, and trains 31 residents and four accredited fellowships with 12 fellows. We are extremely proud of the Obstetrics and Gynecology Research Network ( OGRN ), a research infrastructure that provides comprehensive administrative services and research staffing across multiple hospital and clinician offices. The OGRN facilitates clinical research in our specialty and merits substantial NIH and other extramural funding. The University of Utah Health system has been consistently recognized for excellence in patient care and quality. In September 2025, it was honored as a top performer in the Bernard A. Birnbaum, MD, Quality Leadership Study by Vizient, Inc., marking its 16th consecutive year of such recognition. Additionally, University of Utah Health ranked fourth nationally in Vizient’s Ambulatory Care Quality and Accountability Awards, maintaining a top-ten position for eleven consecutive years. U.S. News & World Report’s 2025-2026 Best Hospitals Rankings placed University of Utah Hospital as the number one hospital in Utah for the 12th consecutive year. Furthermore, the John A. Moran Eye Center secured the 9th spot nationally for ophthalmology care, and the Craig H. Neilsen Rehabilitation Hospital ranked 34th for rehabilitation care. In Newsweek’s World’s Best Hospitals 2024 rankings, University of Utah Hospital was ranked 34th in the United States. These accolades underscore the institution’s unwavering commitment to delivering high-quality patient care and maintaining a culture of excellence. The Utah OB/ GYN Academic Specialist Division currently consists of 25 OB/GYNs, including minimally invasive gynecologic surgeons. The Department also offers a Women’s Global Health two-year fellowship that is typically occupied by an OB/ GYN specialist and currently has a funded K12 Scholar. Our state-of-the-art facilities in Salt Lake City, Utah, include a main hospital campus with inpatient and outpatient operating rooms and multiple community clinics across the Salt Lake Valley. The Division Director will be a key leader in the ongoing development of patient-centered care, with anticipated growth into the community setting, with the ongoing building of a new outpatient and inpatient facility in West Valley, and further anticipated growth with a new hospital planned in Draper, UT. The Director of the Academic Specialist Division of the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Utah will provide leadership, oversight, and direction to the faculty, staff, and trainees in clinical care, education, and research. The Division Director is expected to have an emphasis on clinical and/or foundational research and work in a highly collaborative manner with all clinical, educational, and research leaders. Working with the Chair, the Division Director will focus on improving, developing, and implementing quality monitoring of clinical services. The Division Director will have fiscal and budgetary responsibility for the Division and will plan annually with the Department Chair and the executive committee to determine quality, productivity, expense, and margin targets. This position will offer a high degree of autonomy, as well as ample opportunities for collaboration and challenges. Principle Duties and Responsibilities 1. The Division Director will manage the administrative, clinical, teaching, research, and service activities of the Division, including personnel, operations, and finances. 2. Develop short, intermediate and long-term goals with implementation plans designed to position the department and division as a national leader in clinical care, education, and research. 3. The Division Director will be a key leader in the development of a patient-centered care initiative that will encompass all aspects of OB/ GYN care. 4. Recruit, energize, and retain existing high-caliber faculty, staff, and trainees into the current healthcare paradigm. 5. Demonstrate commitment to fiscally sound management and prudent allocation of available resources. The Director will develop and monitor appropriate deliverables and accountabilities for the faculty, staff, and trainees. 6. Develop entrepreneurial and extramural funding opportunities for the Division. 7. Identify and promote initiatives, programs, and specialized services that will distinguish the Specialist Division as well as specialized services that attract physician and patient self-referrals. 8. Supervise all OB/ GYN Specialist Clinics. 9. Strengthen educational programs and mentoring for trainees. 10. Participate in medical student clerkship instruction, resident and fellow supervision and instruction, and journal clubs. 11. Expand the actively funded research programs within the division with the goal of increasing extramural research funding. 12. Oversee the conduct of NIH and industry-sponsored clinical studies related to OB/ GYN . 13. Develop and implement mentoring and career development processes, including research projects, for all new hires as well as for current faculty. 14. Develop positive working relationships with the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology faculty, administrative leadership, other Division Directors and Vice Chairs, as well as with the leadership of satellite clinical sites, hospital partners and the University of Utah Medical Group ( UUMG ). 15. Promote the Division of Academic Specialists as a national leader in clinical care, research and continuing medical education. 16. Attend Divisional Faculty Meetings, Divisional Patient Care Advisory Meetings, Departmental weekly staff meetings, Departmental Executive Committee meetings, M&M conferences, and Grand Rounds. 17. Serve as the point of contact for Public Relations on issues related to OB/ GYN . Required Skills and Abilities 1. Excellent written and verbal communication skills 2. Engaging leadership style 3. Deep commitment to the trifold mission of clinical care, research, and education 4. Financial competencies in planning, budgeting, control, and organization, 5. Ability to operationalize a comprehensive mission and vision plan Minimum Level of Preparation and Training 1. MD or DO from an accredited institution 2. Board certification in Obstetrics & Gynecology 3. Associate or Professor level 4. Documented evidence of administrative leadership skills Reporting Relationship 1. Chair/Co-Chairs, Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology Effort Distribution 1. 20% Administrative 2. 80% Research and Clinical Activities The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working with students and a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. The University of Utah Health is a patient-focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. The University of Utah values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. For more information, please contact: Cherie.connolly@hsc.utah.edu https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/205056 EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Open Date 07/08/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04081F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). One measure of faculty diversity at the School of Medicine is the proportion of faculty members who come from a rural background. Did you graduate high school from a town with less than 10,000 persons? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
