      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Nocturnist Hospitalist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Nocturnist Hospitalist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Nocturnist Hospitalist Department 00232 - General Internal Medicine City Salt Lake City, UT Track Non Tenure Track New Position to Begin upon hire Details The Department of Internal Medicine, Division of General Internal Medicine at the University of Utah is seeking candidates for a faculty position as a Nocturnist Hospitalist in the clinical track. Faculty rank is dependent upon the qualifications of the applicant. We are an extremely high-performing, low-turnover hospital medicine group that is passionate about teaching and about hospital medicine as a career. Highlights of this position include: Diverse and complex patient mix at an academic medical center drawing from a five-state region of the Mountain West Opportunities to work with a variety of learners including internal medicine residents. Very reasonable clinical workload and schedule allows for outstanding patient care, desirable work/life balance, and a fulfilling long-term career Choose between multiple practice settings: tertiary academic center, nationally-recognized NCI -Designated Comprehensive Cancer Center, community hospitals Extensive career possibilities within the group allow the individual to shape 