    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/211566": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in AI Literacies and Emerging Technologies",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Assistant Professor in AI Literacies and Emerging Technologies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor in AI Literacies and Emerging Technologies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Proposed Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Department 00095 - Dept of Writing and Rhetoric City Salt Lake City, UT Track Tenure Track New Position to Begin 07/01/2027 Details Tenure Track Hire in AI Literacies and Emerging Technologies, Writing and Rhetoric Studies The University of Utah’s Department of Writing & Rhetoric Studies is seeking a tenure­ track assistant professor with a specialization in generative artificial intelligence (AI) and other emerging technologies. Successful candidates will have expertise in AI as it intersects with writing, ethics, pedagogy, and academic research. Secondary expertise in writing program administration, WAC / WID , and/or professional and technical writing are particularly welcome. We invite applications from both early career and experienced scholars. Candidates with established research agendas and a publishing record related to AI are especially encouraged to apply. The regular teaching responsibility is two courses per semester, with release time for taking on substantive administrative roles within the department over time. This faculty position starts in July 2027. Minimum Qualifications PhD in Rhetoric and Composition or closely related field. The degree must be awarded before July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate an ability to conduct and publish high-quality scholarship in writing, rhetoric, and/or literacy studies, to be successful in teaching at both undergraduate and graduate levels, and to work with students of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education for historically underrepresented students. Department Overview The successful candidate will join a dynamic department with a long-standing first-year writing program, a vibrant undergraduate major and minor in Writing & Rhetoric Studies, undergraduate certificates in Medical and Professional and Technical Writing, Masters and PhD programs in Rhetoric and Composition, and a University Writing Center. In 2027, the department anticipates launching a new graduate certificate and online MS degree in Teaching Reading & Writing at Access-Oriented Institutions as well as a Professional MA in Workplace Writing & Emerging Technologies. As a department, we embrace interdisciplinary approaches to writing and rhetoric studies, and we are deeply committed to supporting diverse scholarly interests and methodologies, valuing global rhetorical traditions and language practices, structuring opportunities for students of all backgrounds and identities to learn and grow, and promoting reciprocal relationships with two- and four-year institutions throughout our region and with both local and global communities. The Department of Writing & Rhetoric Studies is housed with the College of Humanities , which fosters many opportunities for critical interdisciplinary scholarship through units like the Tanner Humanities Center , the Asia Center , the Middle East Center , the Center for Latin American Studies , and the Center for Pasifika Indigenous Knowledges . The University also supports AI-related research and teaching across the disciplines through its Responsible AI Initiative . Located in Salt Lake City, the University of Utah is an integral part of a diverse urban region and a state that is home to eight federally recognized tribal nations. The University of Utah is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer and does not discriminate based upon race, national origin, color, religion, sex, age, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, status as a person with a disability, genetic information, or Protected Veteran status. Individuals from historically underrepresented groups, such as minorities, women, qualified persons with disabilities and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. To inquire about the University’s nondiscrimination or affirmative action policies or to request disability accommodation, please contact: Director, Office of Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action, 201 S. Presidents Circle, Rm 135, (801) 581-8365. Application Materials Candidates should submit the following materials no later than October 25, 2026: 1) letter of application; 2) CV; 3) list of references 4) teaching philosophy; 5) writing sample of no more than 25 pages. Candidates who advance beyond the initial screening will be contacted by November 9. Initial interviews will be conducted remotely in November. Campus interviews will begin in December 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Inquiries can be directed to Dr. Jenny Andrus, Chair of the Department of Writing and Rhetoric Studies (j.andrus@utah.edu). EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Candidates should submit the following materials no later than October 25, 2026: 1) letter of application; 2) CV; 3) list of references 4) teaching philosophy; 5) writing sample of no more than 25 pages. Open Date 09/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN01590CF Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Writing Sample 1 List of References Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/211541": {
      "title": "Palliative Care Psychologist",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Palliative Care Psychologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Palliative Care Psychologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Palliative Care Psychologist Department 00232 - General Internal Medicine City Salt Lake City, UT Track Non Tenure Track New Position to Begin Upon Hire Details The University of Utah Palliative Care Services Program, within the Department of Internal Medicine, Division of General Internal Medicine, invites applications for a psychologist position in our adult palliative care clinic located in Salt Lake City, Utah. This is a Clinical Attending faculty appointment on the adjunct track within the Spencer Fox Eccles School of Medicine at the University of Utah. Since its establishment in 2006, our program has been dedicated to providing specialty palliative care for patients with a wide range of serious illnesses. We seek a psychologist who is passionate about delivering high-quality, interdisciplinary palliative care as part of a collaborative team that includes physicians, advanced practice providers, nurses, social workers, and chaplains. The psychologist will provide psychological assessment and evidence-based interventions for patients with serious illness and their families within an outpatient palliative care setting. The psychologist will collaborate closely with other interdisciplinary team members to address the psychological, emotional, behavioral, and psychosocial aspects of serious illness. Opportunities are available to participate in trainee education, program development, quality improvement initiatives, and scholarly activities consistent with the candidate’s interests and program needs. Required Qualifications: PhD or PsyD from an APA -accredited graduate program in clinical, counseling, or health psychology Licensure as a psychologist in the State of Utah At least one year of supervised clinical experience in psychotherapy, health psychology, behavioral medicine, or related clinical practice Demonstrated experience or training in working with patients with chronic, serious, or life-limiting medical conditions Completion of an APA -accredited doctoral internship Eligible for board certification by the American Board of Professional Psychology ( ABPP ) and willing to obtain ABPP board certification within 3 years of appointment Preferred Qualifications: Experience in palliative care, oncology, hospice, or other medical settings Experience delivering evidence-based psychotherapies(e.g., CBT , ACT , meaning-centered therapy, supportive therapy) to individuals and families coping with illness, grief, and loss Experience conducting capacity assessments, behavioral health screenings, and psychosocial evaluation sin medical populations Experience working within interdisciplinary teams(physicians, nurses, social work, chaplaincy, etc.) Two or more years of post-licensure clinical experience, with interest inclinical supervision and the education of trainees Why Join Us? The Supportive and Palliative Care Services Program is committed to fostering an inclusive and stimulating academic environment. We offer a competitive compensation package and professional growth opportunities within a collegial and supportive workplace. Salt Lake City offers an outstanding quality of life in a metropolitan area of 1.26 million residents. Nestled in the foothills of the Wasatch Mountains, the city provides unparalleled access to world-class outdoor recreation, including skiing, hiking, and mountain biking. It boasts a thriving arts and cultural scene with theater, music, and professional sports. More information about life in Utah can be found at https://uofuhealth.utah.edu/living-in-utah . Please apply online including a CV and letter of interest here: https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/211464 . Inquires may be sent to: Cari Low, MD, FACP , c/o Enrique Gonzalez at enrique.gonzalez@hsc.utah.edu . University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Please submit CV with mm/yyyy format for start/end dates. Open Date 10/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04169F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this position? University of Utah Web Page Internet: search engine, online job board, etc. University of Utah employee referral Career Services / Campus Job Fair Community / Government Agency Other / Unknown One measure of faculty diversity at the School of Medicine is the proportion of faculty members who come from a rural background. Did you graduate high school from a town with less than 10,000 persons? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/211535": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Games and Human Values",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Assistant Professor in Games and Human Values Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor in Games and Human Values Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Proposed Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Department 01508 - Games City Salt Lake City, UT Track Tenure Track New Position to Begin 7/1/2027 Details The Division of Games at the University of Utah invites applications for a tenure-line Assistant Professor in Games, with a focus on games and human values, to begin July 1, 2027. This hire is part of the PRESS PLAY Initiative (https://games.utah.edu/pressplay/), a $25 million, multi-year investment by the University of Utah in the faculty, facilities, and programs of the Division of Games. PRESS PLAY is growing both our teaching faculty and our research faculty, and new colleagues will help shape the next stage of games education and research at the U. We seek a scholar whose research examines the nature and value of games and play. We are especially interested in candidates working in the aesthetics and philosophy of games: the ontology of games, the value of play in individual and social contexts, and how games relate to other art forms, including digital and interactive art. Relevant approaches include aesthetics and the philosophy of art from the analytic tradition that complement our existing strengths in that area. The successful candidate will build an externally recognized research program and will teach undergraduate and graduate courses on games, which may include topics in aesthetics, ethics, the philosophy of games, and/or critical play. They will mentor graduate students and work with Division leadership and faculty to strengthen the study of games as a cultural and human practice across our curriculum. We welcome candidates whose work connects with our collaborative efforts with the Department of Philosophy, the Kahlert School of Computing, the College of Fine Arts, the other units within the College of Architecture and Planning, or the University’s planned Institute for Digital Experience. Necessary Qualifications A PhD or equivalent terminal degree in philosophy, aesthetics, or a related field related to the philosophy of games, by the start date Broad knowledge of games as a medium and of game development practice, sufficient to teach in-person courses across the Division’s undergraduate and graduate curricula on the Salt Lake City campus Demonstrated depth of expertise in games and human values, the aesthetics of games, and the philosophy of games Evidence of research productivity appropriate to career stage and progression, such as publications in leading games, philosophy, or aesthetics venues Demonstrated commitment to teaching and/or mentoring undergraduate and graduate students in lectures, seminars, and/or studio simulations Demonstrated potential to contribute to university and professional service, such as collaborative curriculum development, outreach to local industry and government partners, or recruitment Preferred Qualifications Research in the aesthetics of games, the philosophy of art, the nature of play and interactivity, or the value of games An understanding of game development practice, or experience making games Experience using games as objects of critical analysis in the classroom Ability to develop new courses in emerging areas of games scholarship About the Division The Division of Games, in the College of Architecture + Planning, is a world leader in games education, with consistently top-ranked programs at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The Utah Games faculty includes artists, philosophers, games studies scholars, designers, and computer scientists who collectively work together on the mission to push the boundaries of what is possible in games. This plurality of backgrounds is one of the core elements within our identity. We strongly value inter- and transdisciplinary approaches to research and education, and seek to foster collaboration across the University of Utah. Currently, our faculty sustain ongoing collaborations with other departments within our College of Architecture and Planning, as well as the School of Medicine, the Colleges of Education, Humanities, Science and Engineering, and other campus partners. The University of Utah has remarkable strengths between the Division of Games and the Department of Philosophy targeting scholarship in the philosophy of games. Additionally, we maintain strong collaborations with the vibrant local game development community and other significant game industry-wide partners. Our unit is committed to being a responsible member of our campus and professional community, and we strive to recruit and support faculty committed to acting in furtherance of our unit’s values. Interested candidates may view these values by visiting https://games.utah.edu/utah-games-values/ If you are interested in joining us to build a culture of academic excellence; to create ideas that advance our understanding of games; to share those ideas with our students, communities, and society; and to apply those ideas to change the world for the better, we strongly encourage you to apply. About the College of Architecture and Planning The University of Utah College of Architecture and Planning (CA+P) is a community of award-winning faculty, entrepreneurial students, and support staff that together form a creative community unlike any other. The College is home to four academic units: the School of Architecture, the Department of City and Metropolitan Planning, the Division of Games, and the Division of Multi-Disciplinary Design, as well as multiple research centers and collaboratives. Across these units are top-ranked academic programs, outstanding researchers with a strong commitment to addressing defining issues of our time, and a record of unsurpassed societal impact. As part of a campus that values innovation and interdisciplinarity, the College is transforming its disciplines and training graduates to become leaders and changemakers in the built and virtual environments globally. More information is available at cap.utah.edu. About the University of Utah The University of Utah is a Carnegie Research I institution located in Salt Lake City, nestled in the breathtaking foothills of the Wasatch Mountains. With thriving arts and culinary scenes, and an exploding high technology sector, Salt Lake City offers a unique mix of urban life juxtaposed with access to remarkable national parks, ski resorts, hiking and climbing, and more, just minutes away from campus. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates All qualified individuals are strongly encouraged to apply. Review of applications will begin immediately and proceed until the position is filled. The position will start July 1, 2027, depending on the timing of hiring and availability of the candidate. Application Materials To apply, candidates must submit the following materials: Current CV Cover letter describing your interest in the position, identifying the area(s) of expertise for which you wish to be considered in evaluation and summarizing your research expertise and personal academic goals. A Teaching Statement that addresses your experience and plans for teaching and student mentoring. A Research Statement describing your current and planned research specific to the research areas described above. Up to three publications representing your relevant scholarship. Contact information for three references. These materials should make clear how the applicant meets each of the necessary qualifications for the position and, at the candidate’s discretion, how the applicant meets our preferred qualifications beyond the necessary ones. Open Date 10/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN01602CF Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only Example of Research 1 Example of Research 2 Example of Research 3 University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/211605": {
      "title": "Nurse Midwifery/Women&#39;s Health Nurse Practitioner Career-Line Faculty Positions",
      "description": "University of Utah Employment Site | Nurse Midwifery/Women&#39;s Health Nurse Practitioner Career-Line Faculty Positions Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Nurse Midwifery/Women's Health Nurse Practitioner Career-Line Faculty Positions Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details The University of Utah, an AA/EO employer, encourages applications from all qualified individuals, and provides reasonable accommodation to the known disabilities of applicants and employees. The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students, staff, faculty and patients from all backgrounds and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education, employment opportunities, and quality healthcare for historically underrepresented groups. Position Information Position/Rank Career Line Faculty (rank DOQ) Department 00989 - CON - GEAP DIVISION City Salt Lake City, UT Track Non Tenure Track New Position to Begin ASAP Details The University of Utah College of Nursing invites applications for a career-line (non-tenure-track) faculty position with primary teaching responsibilities in the Nurse Midwifery and Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner emphases within the Doctor of Nursing Practice program. Academic rank is dependent on qualifications. Principal Functions and Responsibilities: This career-line faculty member will primarily assume teaching responsibilities in the Doctor of Nursing Practice ( DNP ) Nurse Midwifery and Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner emphases. Responsibilities include classroom and/or online didactic instruction, supervision of students in DNP Scholarly Project courses, and clinical supervision of students in the Nurse Midwifery and Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner emphases. The faculty member will also provide ongoing assessment, feedback, and guidance regarding student performance and progression through their programs of study. Additional teaching opportunities may be available based on qualifications, certification, interests, and course availability. Other faculty responsibilities include contributing to program and curriculum development for both emphases, participating in College committees, and engaging in professional activities and service, as negotiated through individual workload assignments. Participation in clinically focused scholarship is expected and is an important component of long-term retention and advancement in academic rank. Criteria: Candidates must be graduates of an accredited college or school of nursing and hold a Doctor of Nursing Practice ( DNP ) or Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) degree. Applicants must hold a current Utah Advanced Practice Registered Nurse ( APRN ) license and/or Certified Nurse Midwifery license or be eligible for licensure in the State of Utah. Utah is a Nurse Licensure Compact state. Candidates must also hold national certification in the Nurse Midwifery ( CNM ) and/or Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner ( WHNP ) specialty areas. Clinical expertise as a Nurse Midwife and/or Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner is required. Relevant healthcare experience, demonstrated clinical expertise, and strong organizational and communication skills are essential. Teaching experience in classroom, clinical, and simulation settings is preferred. Candidates must also possess excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with patients and members of healthcare and academic teams. Candidates must possess strong leadership, management, organizational, and communication skills, along with the ability to collaborate effectively and productively with faculty, students, healthcare professionals, and other academic and clinical stakeholders. Teaching experience in classroom, clinical, and simulation settings is preferred. Applicants must be willing to reside in Utah and work on-site at the College of Nursing and/or healthcare facilities throughout the Salt Lake Valley. The College of Nursing: The CON is an integral part of University of Utah Health. We are committed to working together to serve the people of Utah and beyond by continually improving individual and community health and quality of life. We strive for excellence in education, research, and clinical care, with each mission being vital to the others and to our overall success. Acceptance, integrity, independent inquiry, and collegiality form the fabric of everyday life for faculty and students. Please visit the College of Nursing website to learn more about the College. The University of Utah: The University of Utah is a Big 12 institution located in Salt Lake City nestled in the foothills of the Wasatch Mountains. Please visit the following webpages for more information about the University of Utah, Faculty Careers at the University of Utah, and Living in Utah. Application and Inquiries : Interested candidate should apply online at https://utah.peopleadmin.com/postings/211435 . The application requires: 1) curriculum vitae, 2) cover letter, and 3) three letters of recommendation from individuals external to the University of Utah and U of U Health. Please note that letters must be signed, dated and on letterhead. For additional information: Please contact Deidre Schoenfeld, Director of the Office of Faculty Affairs & Division Services at deidre.schoenfeld@nurs.utah.edu or Dr. Linda Hofmann, Chair of the Division of Graduate Education and Advanced Practice at linda.hofmann@nurs.utah.edu. University of Utah employees are expected to live and work in the state of Utah. The University of Utah Health (U of U Health) is a patient-focused center distinguished by collaboration, excellence, leadership, and respect. The U of U Health values candidates who are committed to fostering and furthering the culture of compassion, collaboration, innovation, accountability, acceptance, integrity, quality, and trust that is integral to our mission. EEO/Non-Discrimination Information The University of Utah values candidates who have experience working in settings with students and possess a strong commitment to improving access to higher education. Veterans’ preference is extended to qualified applicants, upon request and consistent with University policy and Utah state law. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Consistent with state and federal law, the University of Utah does not discriminate based upon race, ethnicity, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, or protected veteran’s status. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, as required by Title IX and 34 CFR part 106. The requirement not to discriminate in education programs or activities extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its regulations may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, to the Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, or both. To request a reasonable accommodation for a disability or if you or someone you know has experienced discrimination or sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, you may contact the Director/Title IX Coordinator in the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX ( OEO ). More information, including the Director/Title IX Coordinator’s office address, electronic mail address, and telephone number, can be located at https://www.utah.edu/nondiscrimination/ . Online reports may be submitted at https://oeo.utah.edu . Notice The University is a participating employer with Utah Retirement Systems (“URS”). Eligible new hires with prior URS service, may elect to enroll in URS if they make the election before they become eligible for retirement (usually the first day of work). Contact Human Resources at (801) 581-7447 for information. Individuals who previously retired and are receiving monthly retirement benefits from URS are subject to URS’ post-retirement rules and restrictions. Please contact Utah Retirement Systems at (801) 366-7770 or (800) 695-4877 or University Human Resource Management at (801) 581-7447 if you have questions regarding the post-retirement rules. This position may require the successful completion of a criminal background check and/or drug screen. https://publicsafety.utah.edu/safetyreport/ This report includes statistics about criminal offenses, hate crimes, arrests and referrals for disciplinary action, and Violence Against Women Act offenses. They also provide information about safety and security-related services offered by the University of Utah. A paper copy can be obtained by request at the Department of Public Safety located at 1658 East 500 South. Special Instructions for Candidates Open Date 10/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Requisition Number PRN04165F Type Faculty Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Optional Documents Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Description for More Information – Appropriate discharge document (such as DD-2214) – Veteran Only Historical Only – Do Not Use – See Document Description for More Information – Addendum to the University of Utah – Veteran Only Teaching Statement University Human Resource Management 250 East 200 South, Suite 125 Salt Lake City, UT 84111 Contact us: (801) 581-2169 By Email: employment@utah.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
